		(property "Description" "Realtek RTL8125BG-CG, 2.5GbE PCIe NIC, QFN-48-EP 6x6mm. Pin table (all 48 signal pins + EP) verified against RTL8125BG(S)-CG datasheet Rev 1.5 (leaked NDA doc, cross-checked pin-for-pin against Realtek's own published reference schematic V122 and 4 shipping Radxa boards -- see task-10-report.md Sources). PERSTB/CLKREQB/LANWAKEB are 3.3V-only (VIH min 2.0V per Table 29) -- NOT 1.8V tolerant (Realtek removed 1.8V I/O compat at Rev 1.1); level-shifted from the m2 sheet's +1V8 domain on this sheet (Q36-38, BSS138). Fix pass 2026-07-15: pin 15 renamed AVDD33_PLL per reference V122 (bead-isolated PLL supply); BG (non-S) variant kept -- BGS not orderable (no LCSC/authorized listing) -- so 0.95V core comes from an external buck enabled by POW_EXT_SWR pin 6, per datasheet Table 5/Table 11 and reference page 4 'Power Module for External Core Power'. 3.3V domain fed by dedicated +3V3_ETH forced-PWM 1.2MHz buck per reference notice '3.3V from switching regulator must be PWM mode and Freq>=1Mhz'. Sourced: LCSC C3013605." (at 0 0 0) (hide yes) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		(property "ki_keywords" "RTL8125 2.5GbE PCIe NIC ethernet" (at 0 0 0) (hide yes) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
